  "id": "COMPOUND:11293 - PROTEIN:3990",
  "verbalization": "Fenpiprane is implicated in targeting Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is a key player in the regulation of cellular processes. This protein is also a target of Ugonin S and Cyclohexanone, a structural analog, all of which ultimately lead to the Inner centromere protein. The evidence suggests that Fenpiprane may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, which is a central component in the pathway leading to the Inner centromere protein. The presence of multiple targets of Multidrug resistance-associated protein 7, including Ugonin S and Cyclohexanone, indicates that the protein may act as a bridge in the signaling cascade that ultimately influences the Inner centromere protein. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Fenpiprane to modulate cellular processes through this protein, suggesting a broader role in cellular regulation.",
